  "paras": [
   "USDA&rsquo;s 2027 county base values, the same on every grid in the county. Protection per acre is the value times your coverage level times a productivity factor of 60 to 150: grazing at 90% and 100 is $7.83 an acre.",
   "At 90% coverage, across the grids that touch the county that price each pair of months (104 in all; a row priced on fewer says how many): first the middle grid for that pair of months (it can be a different grid in each row), then the lowest and highest. The premium is the full rate per $100 of protection; USDA pays 59% at 70%, 59% at 75%, 55% at 80%, 55% at 85%, 51% at 90%. Normal is the grid&rsquo;s average precipitation for those months. A year counts, of the 75 from 1951 to 2025, when the grid&rsquo;s index for those months came in under 90% of normal, which is when a 90% policy pays.",
   "The wettest pair of months here is January to February (1.67 in on the middle of the 104 grids) and the driest is May to June (0.14 in). Coverage costs least in July to August and most in May to June. The months to insure are the ones when a dry spell costs you grass or hay, not the cheapest ones.",
   "The index for each pair of months as a percent of normal (100 is a normal year), on the middle of the 104 grids (each grid has its own; the calculator shows yours). Shaded cells came in under 90%, where a 90% policy on those months would have paid. 2026 shows the 6 pairs of months USDA has published so far.",
   "Each grid&rsquo;s normal precipitation over a year, its driest year since 1951 as a percent of normal, 2025 as a percent of normal, and how many of 75 years as a whole came in under 90%.",
   "And 74 more grids: 17162, 17163, 17164, 17450, 17451, 17452, 17453, 17454, 17455, 17456, 17457, 17458, 17459, 17460, 17461, 17462, 17463, 17750, 17751, 17752, 17753, 17754, 17755, 17756, 17757, 17758, 17759, 17760, 17761, 17762, 18050, 18051, 18052, 18053, 18054, 18055, 18056, 18057, 18058, 18059, 18060, 18061, 18062, 18350, 18351, 18352, 18353, 18354, 18355, 18356, 18357, 18358, 18359, 18360, 18361, 18650, 18651, 18652, 18653, 18654, 18655, 18656, 18657, 18658, 18659, 18950, 18951, 18952, 18953, 18954, 18955, 18956, 18957, 18958. Each opens in the <a href=\"/prf?c=06071\" rel=\"nofollow\">calculator</a>."
  ]
 },
